THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

The MIT License above applies to the original work of LyMeowz Shader.

Some techniques and code fragments in this pack are adapted from, or based on,
the public works listed below. They are credited in the source comments and
remain the property of their respective authors. They are NOT relicensed by
the MIT License above, and may be covered by their own licenses (for example,
Shadertoy code is often CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 unless its author states otherwise).
The licenses of these works have not been verified here; check each source
before redistributing or using this pack commercially.

  - afl_ext, "Very fast procedural ocean" (https://www.shadertoy.com/view/MdXyzX)
    -> shaders/lib/water/waterNormal.glsl
  - piyushslayer, "Happy 2020!" (https://www.shadertoy.com/view/tt3GRN)
    -> moon rendering in shaders/lib/atmosphere/celestial.glsl
  - hornet, "Texture Filtering: Catmull-Rom" (https://www.shadertoy.com/view/MtVGWz)
    and simesgreen (https://www.shadertoy.com/view/4df3Dn)
    -> shaders/lib/camera/filter.glsl
  - https://www.shadertoy.com/view/McVXWR
    -> shaders/lib/antialiasing/anisotropicFiltering.glsl
  - dmnsgn/glsl-tone-map (https://github.com/dmnsgn/glsl-tone-map)
    -> AgX tone mapping in shaders/lib/camera/toneMapping.glsl
  - AMD FidelityFX FSR (RCAS), via https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/637639295
    -> shaders/lib/antialiasing/FSR.glsl
  - Morgan McGuire and Michael Mara, "Efficient GPU Screen-Space Ray Tracing",
    JCGT vol. 3 no. 4, 2014 -> shaders/lib/lighting/rayTracing.glsl
  - Activision, "Practical Real-Time Strategies for Accurate Indirect Occlusion"
    -> GTAO in shaders/lib/lighting/SSAO.glsl
  - Jimenez et al. octahedral normal encoding ("A Survey of Efficient
    Representations for Independent Unit Vectors", JCGT 2014)
    -> shaders/lib/common/normal.glsl
  - BSL Shaders (TBN matrix construction approach, referenced in gbuffers programs)
  - Articles credited in source comments (Zhihu, CSDN, Feishu): TAA, bloom,
    depth of field, height fog, volumetric clouds, noise library, subsurface
    scattering, parallax mapping, stars (a_codecat).

If you are the author of any of the above and want a credit changed or a
fragment removed, please open an issue.
